  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Starting from the Lavandou harbour, this coastal trail follows the coast to Plage de la Fossette, with lovely views of the islands of Port-Cros and Levant. Easy as far as Plage de Saint-Clair, it gets more demanding after that.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>⚠️ Important: dogs are banned from all of Le Lavandou's beaches from 1 April to 31 October, even on a leash. Some tolerance only exists out of season, from November to March. The trail itself, away from the beaches, remains usable all year round. The stretch between Saint-Clair and La Fossette is more technical, with unsecured sections.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: save this walk for autumn, winter or very early spring if you want to enjoy the trail with your dog without beach restrictions.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Le Lavandou and its harbour are right nearby, with views of the islands of Port-Cros and Levant offshore.</p>
    </div>

